---
// Moving between the site's pages without a full page load: Astro's client router, which fetches
// the next page, swaps it in for this one, and keeps the back and forward buttons working. It is in
// the head of every page, since a page without it is left by a full page load. A link still works
// as an ordinary link with scripts off: the router only takes over a click it can handle.
//
// An island is torn down by Astro when its page is swapped out, and one on the next page is
// hydrated there. A custom element starts and stops on its own. Where a navigation goes is the
// reader's trail's to say (TrailSpines.astro), which sends each one to the address of the trail it
// makes.
import { ClientRouter } from "astro:transitions"
---

<ClientRouter />
